{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FIX FOR THE CELL'S RED IS UP: Gerrit 1231 (the diagnosis pin, tests only) and 1232 (the fix,\n`inbound_differ` + `apply_inbound_records` + tests), stacked. Both carry\n`rebar-ticket: 8d68-a740-4f56-4b3a` / 5200 respectively; the mechanism, RED->GREEN evidence and\nboth mutation verdicts are recorded on [rebar:8d68-a740-4f56-4b3a].\n\nWHAT IT MEANS FOR THIS STORY: J11's `test_the_inbound_assignee_mints_a_jira_family_identity`\nshould go green on the next harness run WITHOUT any change to the cell — the oracle, its setup\nsteps and every assertion stay exactly as they are on main. The cell was right; the product was\nnot. That is the outcome the rewrite was for: it found a real defect that the previous,\ntautological version could not have surfaced (and did not, across four harness runs).\n\nCI NOTE for whoever watches the next run: `Verified -1` on 1231 came from the\n`pip-audit (dependency vulnerabilities)` job, not from the test suite. It passed on 1226/1227\ntwo hours earlier, fails now on BOTH 1231 (tests-only) and 1232 (src+tests) — two unrelated\nchangesets, neither adding a dependency — and `pip-audit` run locally against this checkout\nreports \"No known vulnerabilities found\". Treated as a flake and `recheck` posted."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785711054101959001,"uuid":"983c0867-4d00-4007-b638-72e1bebaadda"}